From: WOZIWRT <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt76-vendor: send the air-monitor MAC as six bytes, not as a nest

`mt76-vendor <dev> set amnt <idx> <mac>` has always failed with

    nl80211 call failed: Invalid argument

on our tree. The tool and the driver disagree about one attribute:
amnt_set_policy declares MTK_VENDOR_ATTR_AMNT_SET_MACADDR as
NLA_POLICY_EXACT_LEN_WARN(ETH_ALEN), so it must carry exactly six bytes, while
the tool nests six u8 attributes inside it - roughly 48 bytes once headers and
padding are counted. The policy check then rejects the whole message.

Nothing says so out loud. The driver rejects silently (dmesg stays empty) and
the reason travels in extack, which this tool does not print, so all the user
sees is EINVAL.

Send it flat. Diagnosed 2026-09-01 by reading both sides against
0053-mtk-mt76-mt7996-add-vendor-support.patch.

Worth having: amnt is the only way to measure the signal of stations we are NOT
associated with - up to sixteen of them, per antenna chain - which is how a node
can weigh candidate parents before moving its backhaul instead of after.

Signed-off-by: WOZIWRT <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/feed/app/mt76-vendor/src/amnt.c
+++ b/feed/app/mt76-vendor/src/amnt.c
@@ -19,9 +19,9 @@
 
 static int mt76_amnt_set_attr(struct nl_msg *msg, int argc, char **argv)
 {
-	void *tb1, *tb2;
+	void *tb1;
 	u8 a[ETH_ALEN], idx;
-	int i = 0, matches;
+	int matches;
 
 	idx = strtoul(argv[0], NULL, 0);
 	matches = sscanf(argv[1], "%hhx:%hhx:%hhx:%hhx:%hhx:%hhx",
@@ -36,16 +36,21 @@
 
 	nla_put_u8(msg, MTK_VENDOR_ATTR_AMNT_SET_INDEX, idx);
 
-	tb2 = nla_nest_start(msg, MTK_VENDOR_ATTR_AMNT_SET_MACADDR | NLA_F_NESTED);
-	if (!tb2) {
-		nla_nest_end(msg, tb1);
-		return -ENOMEM;
-	}
-
-	for (i = 0; i < ETH_ALEN; i++)
-		nla_put_u8(msg, i, a[i]);
+	/* Flat six bytes, not a nest of six u8 attributes.
+	 *
+	 * The driver validates this with NLA_POLICY_EXACT_LEN_WARN(ETH_ALEN)
+	 * (0053-mtk-mt76-mt7996-add-vendor-support.patch, amnt_set_policy), so the
+	 * payload has to be exactly six bytes. Nesting six u8 attributes inside it
+	 * costs a header and padding per byte - about 48 - and the netlink policy
+	 * check rejects the whole message.
+	 *
+	 * The user never learns why: the reason travels in extack, which this tool
+	 * does not print, so `set amnt` failed with nothing but
+	 * "nl80211 call failed: Invalid argument". Diagnosed 2026-09-01 by reading
+	 * both sides; the driver rejects silently, dmesg stays empty.
+	 */
+	nla_put(msg, MTK_VENDOR_ATTR_AMNT_SET_MACADDR, ETH_ALEN, a);
 
-	nla_nest_end(msg, tb2);
 	nla_nest_end(msg, tb1);
 
 	return 0;
